WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 2.8 · Theory of Change
Assumptions, risks and evidence

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Before you launch, almost every link in your pathway rests on assumptions.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:25.170
An assumption is something that must be true for one step in your pathway to lead to the next. Before you launch, almost every link rests on assumptions.

4
00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:26.170
Where assumptions sit

5
00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:35.648
Inputs to activities: Will the resources really be there when needed? For example: The youth centre will keep referring young people for the whole first year.

6
00:00:35.648 --> 00:00:43.644
Activities to outputs: Can people take part as planned? For example: Trainees can reach the kitchen by 7 am on public transport.

7
00:00:43.644 --> 00:00:52.011
Outputs to outcomes: Does what we deliver lead to change? For example: Trainees who finish will feel confident enough to apply for jobs.

8
00:00:52.011 --> 00:01:01.948
Outcomes to impact: Do wider conditions allow the change to last? For example: Local employers will hire young people who complete the bakery’s traineeship.

9
00:01:02.348 --> 00:01:02.948
Why they matter

10
00:01:02.948 --> 00:01:07.511
1. Untested assumptions are where good plans quietly fail.

11
00:01:07.511 --> 00:01:12.815
2. Testing cheaply first saves money you cannot afford to lose.

12
00:01:12.815 --> 00:01:19.489
3. Deciding your response early turns a failed assumption into a lesson.

13
00:01:19.889 --> 00:01:20.489
How you will test them

14
00:01:20.489 --> 00:01:25.793
1. Start with the ones that are both important and uncertain.

15
00:01:25.793 --> 00:01:31.467
2. Test cheaply: ask future participants, check records, run a small pilot.

16
00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:37.770
3. Carry external risks into your risk register in Module 10.

17
00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:38.770
What to avoid

18
00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:44.074
Vague assumptions, like “the project succeeds”, that cannot be checked.

19
00:01:44.074 --> 00:01:48.267
Committing money before testing the riskiest links.

20
00:01:48.267 --> 00:01:54.570
Mixing risks you cannot control with your response to them.

21
00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:56.970
You write your critical assumptions, evidence and how you will test them.

22
00:01:56.970 --> 00:02:00.970
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:05.570
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
